  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Great Apes Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to assess and strengthen the conservation of the yellow-cheeked crested gibbon on the southeastern slope of the Da Lat Plateau. This will be done by: (1) presenting a short training course to the staff of two protected areas and forest rangers of the state forest enterprises on primate classification, ecological and behavioral characteristics of gibbons, listening post survey and line transect survey techniques, and equipment use; (2) providing field experience at the end of the training and introducing a plan to survey specific sites; (3) conducting both listening post surveys and line transect surveys in all suitable habitats; (4) estimating the total population of the two provinces (Ninh Thuan and Khanh Hoa provinces) and identifying the important sites for continued conservation efforts; and (5) presenting a provincial workshop to inform government officials of results of the project and recommend incorporation of project results into conservation planning of the two provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
